---
import ToolPage from '@versal/ui/ToolPage.astro';

const title = "JSON to Zod Schema";
const description = "Infer a Zod validation schema from any JSON sample. Paste your JSON and get a type-safe Zod schema you can copy directly into your project.";
const faqs = [
  {
    "question": "How do I convert JSON to a Zod schema?",
    "answer": "Paste a JSON sample into the input and click Infer Schema. The tool analyses the structure, data types, and nested objects, then generates a TypeScript Zod schema you can copy and use in your project. Optional fields are inferred from null values."
  },
  {
    "question": "Is the generated Zod schema accurate?",
    "answer": "The schema infers types from your sample data. For optional fields, empty arrays, and null values the tool marks them as optional or nullable. For precise type inference, provide a representative JSON sample that covers all fields you want validated."
  }
];
import ToolNav from '@versal/ui/ToolNav.astro';
import BaseLayout from '@versal/ui/BaseLayout';
---

<ToolPage
  site="main"
  title={title}
  description={description}
  canonical="https://jsonversal.com/tools/json-to-zod/"
  current="/tools/json-to-zod/"
  faqs={faqs}
  about={[
    {
      "heading": "Inference rules, including the string heuristics",
      "body": [
        "Beyond the obvious type mapping, the generator sniffs string contents and promotes the result: a bare `YYYY-MM-DD` becomes `z.string().date()`, a value with a date and a time component becomes `z.string().datetime({ offset: true })` — the offset option is what lets a timestamp without a trailing `Z` validate — an address-shaped value becomes `.email()`, and an `http` or `https` prefix becomes `.url()`. All four are guesses from one sample value, so a field that is a URL in this record and a plain string in the next will reject the second.",
        "Numbers become `z.number().int()` when the value is whole, so a field that is sometimes `98` and sometimes `98.5` rejects the fractional case outright — drop the `.int()` if the field is ever fractional. `null` becomes `z.null()` and its property is marked `.nullable()`, which admits null without permitting the key to be missing — add `.optional()` if absence is also legal."
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "How the schema is assembled",
      "body": [
        "Nested objects of any depth are hoisted into their own `const XSchema` declarations, each emitted above the schema that references it, so a document nested three levels deep produces three named schemas and a root that composes them. Names come from capitalising the key and appending `Schema`; two keys that capitalise alike, such as `items` and `Items`, get a numeric suffix rather than colliding. Arrays merge their object elements the same way and become `z.array(ElementSchema)`, and heterogeneous arrays become `z.array(z.union([...]))`. An empty array becomes `z.array(z.unknown())` and an empty object becomes `z.record(z.unknown())`, both of which validate far more than the sample implies.",
        "`Make strict` appends `.strict()` to the outermost schema only — the substitution targets the final closing parenthesis of the output — so nested object schemas keep default behaviour and will silently drop unknown keys instead of rejecting them. Toggling off removes every `.strict()` occurrence, including any you added yourself."
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Where the generated schema stops",
      "body": [
        "`Make strict` appends `.strict()` to the outermost schema only — the substitution targets the final closing parenthesis of the output — so nested object schemas keep default behaviour and will silently drop unknown keys instead of rejecting them. Toggling off removes every `.strict()` occurrence, including any you added yourself.",
        "Zod is the strictest of these validators about unknown keys, which is the point of using it — a schema inferred from one sample will reject any field that sample did not contain. Loosen it with `.partial()`, `.passthrough()`, or explicit optional keys before pointing it at live traffic, or every legitimate addition upstream becomes a validation error."
      ]
    }
  ]}
>

  <section class="card mt-2">
    <h2 class="h2-card">Input JSON</h2>
    <label for="input" class="sr-only">Input</label>
    <textarea id="input" placeholder='&#123;&#10;  "id": 1,&#10;  "name": "Bob",&#10;  "email": "bob@example.com"&#10;&#125;'></textarea>
    <div class="row mt-1">
      <button class="primary" id="convert">Generate Zod Schema</button>
      <button class="ghost" id="sample">Load sample</button>
      <button class="ghost" id="clear">Clear</button>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="card mt-2" id="output-section" style="display:none;">
    <div class="row" style="margin-bottom:12px;">
      <h2 class="h2-flat">Zod Schema</h2>
      <div class="row" style="gap:8px;">
        <button class="ghost" id="copy">Copy</button>
        <button class="ghost" id="strict">Make strict</button>
      </div>
    </div>
    <pre id="output">—</pre>
    <p class="text-dim" style="margin-top:8px;font-size:.85rem;">
      Requires <code>zod</code>  — install with <code>npm install zod</code>
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="card mt-2" id="error-section" style="display:none;">
    <h2 class="h2-error">Error</h2>
    <pre id="error-out" class="mt-1" style="color:var(--danger);">—</pre>
  </section>

  <h2>How it works</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Paste a JSON example representing your expected data shape.</li>
    <li>Click <strong>Generate Zod Schema</strong>  — a ready-to-use Zod schema is produced.</li>
    <li>Copy the schema into your TypeScript project and use it for runtime validation.</li>
    <li>Click <strong>Make strict</strong> to add <code>.strict()</code> and reject unknown keys.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Usage example</h2>
  <pre>import &#123; z &#125; from 'zod';
import &#123; userSchema &#125; from './schemas/user';

const result = userSchema.safeParse(&#123; name: 'Alice', id: 1 &#125;);
if (result.success) &#123;
  console.log(result.data);
&#125; else &#123;
  console.error(result.error.format());
&#125;</pre>

  <h2>About JSON to Zod Schema</h2>
  <p class="text-muted">Zod is a TypeScript-first schema declaration and validation library that checks your data at runtime and infers types at compile time. Because JSON carries no type information beyond its values, inferring a Zod schema from a JSON sample gives you a fast starting point instead of handwriting validators by hand. This tool performs that inference and outputs a schema you can drop straight into your project.</p>
  <p class="text-muted">Use it when you receive data from an external API, a database, or an LLM and want runtime guarantees about its shape. Remember that the inferred schema is only as good as your sample: if the sample is incomplete  — missing optional fields, empty arrays, or null values  — the generated schema may be too narrow or too wide, so review and adjust it before relying on it in production.</p>
</ToolPage>

<style>
  .row { display: flex; align-items: center; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 8px; }
  textarea { min-height: 160px; }
  pre { min-height: 80px; }
  code { font-size: .85rem; }
</style>

<script is:inline>
(function () {
  function capitalize(s) {
    return s.charAt(0).toUpperCase() + s.slice(1);
  }

  // Returns a schema expression for `value`. Any `const XSchema = ...` it needs
  // is appended to `decls`, children before parents, so every identifier the
  // output references is also declared above it.
  function jsonToZod(root, rootName) {
    rootName = rootName || 'Root';
    const decls = [];
    const used = new Set();

    function isPlainObject(v) {
      return v !== null && typeof v === 'object' && !Array.isArray(v);
    }

    function ensureUnique(base) {
      let candidate = base, i = 2;
      while (used.has(candidate)) candidate = base + (i++);
      used.add(candidate);
      return candidate;
    }

    function unique(base) {
      let n = String(base == null ? '' : base).replace(/[^A-Za-z0-9_$]/g, '');
      if (!n || !/^[A-Za-z_$]/.test(n)) n = 'Item' + n;
      n = n.charAt(0).toUpperCase() + n.slice(1);
      if (!/Schema$/.test(n)) n += 'Schema';
      return ensureUnique(n);
    }

    function mergeObjects(objs) {
      const merged = {};
      for (const item of objs) {
        for (const [k, v] of Object.entries(item)) {
          if (!(k in merged)) merged[k] = v;
        }
      }
      return merged;
    }

    function stringSchema(value) {
      if (/^\d{4}-\d{2}-\d{2}$/.test(value)) return 'z.string().date()';
      if (/^\d{4}-\d{2}-\d{2}[Tt ]\d{2}:\d{2}/.test(value)) return 'z.string().datetime({ offset: true })';
      if (/^[^\s@]+@[^\s@]+\.[^\s@]+$/.test(value)) return 'z.string().email()';
      if (/^https?:\/\//.test(value)) return 'z.string().url()';
      return 'z.string()';
    }

    function schemaExpr(value, name) {
      if (value === null) return 'z.null()';
      if (typeof value === 'boolean') return 'z.boolean()';
      if (typeof value === 'number') return Number.isInteger(value) ? 'z.number().int()' : 'z.number()';
      if (typeof value === 'string') return stringSchema(value);
      if (Array.isArray(value)) {
        if (value.length === 0) return 'z.array(z.unknown())';
        const seen = [];
        const objects = [];
        for (const item of value) {
          if (isPlainObject(item)) {
            objects.push(item);
          } else {
            const t = schemaExpr(item, '');
            if (seen.indexOf(t) === -1) seen.push(t);
          }
        }
        if (objects.length > 0) {
          const inner = schemaExpr(mergeObjects(objects), name);
          if (seen.indexOf(inner) === -1) seen.push(inner);
        }
        const joined = seen.length === 1 ? seen[0] : 'z.union([' + seen.join(', ') + '])';
        return 'z.array(' + joined + ')';
      }
      if (isPlainObject(value)) {
        const schemaName = unique(name);
        decls.push('const ' + schemaName + ' = ' + objectSchema(value) + ';');
        return schemaName;
      }
      return 'z.unknown()';
    }

    function objectSchema(obj) {
      const entries = Object.entries(obj);
      if (entries.length === 0) return 'z.record(z.unknown())';
      let s = 'z.object({\n';
      for (const [k, v] of entries) {
        const safeKey = /^[a-zA-Z_$][a-zA-Z0-9_$]*$/.test(k) ? k : JSON.stringify(k);
        const isNull = v === null;
        const t = isNull ? 'z.null()' : schemaExpr(v, capitalize(k));
        s += '  ' + safeKey + ': ' + t + (isNull ? '.nullable()' : '') + ',\n';
      }
      return s + '})';
    }

    const rootSchema = schemaExpr(root, isPlainObject(root) ? rootName : 'Item');
    let out = decls.join('\n\n');
    if (!isPlainObject(root)) {
      // A scalar or array root has no object of its own; emit a named const so
      // the output is a complete, importable schema.
      out = (out ? out + '\n\n' : '') + 'const ' + unique(rootName) + ' = ' + rootSchema + ';';
    }
    return out;
  }

  const $ = (id) => document.getElementById(id);
  const input = $('input');
  const outputSection = $('output-section');
  const errorSection = $('error-section');
  const output = $('output');
  const errorOut = $('error-out');

  $('convert').addEventListener('click', function () {
    const raw = input.value.trim();
    if (!raw) { showToast('Please paste some JSON first.'); return; }
    try {
      const obj = JSON.parse(raw);
      const schema = jsonToZod(obj, 'Root');
      output.textContent = schema;
      outputSection.style.display = 'block';
      errorSection.style.display = 'none';
      $('strict').textContent = 'Make strict';
    } catch (e) {
      errorOut.textContent = e.message;
      errorSection.style.display = 'block';
      outputSection.style.display = 'none';
    }
  });

  $('sample').addEventListener('click', function () {
    input.value = JSON.stringify({
      id: 1,
      name: "Bob",
      email: "bob@example.com",
      age: null,
      scores: [98, 87, 95],
      address: {
        street: "123 Main St",
        city: "New York",
        zip: 10001
      },
      active: true
    }, null, 2);
  });

  $('clear').addEventListener('click', function () {
    input.value = '';
    outputSection.style.display = 'none';
    errorSection.style.display = 'none';
  });

  $('copy').addEventListener('click', async function () {
    try {
      await navigator.clipboard.writeText(output.textContent);
      $('copy').textContent = 'Copied!';
      setTimeout(() => $('copy').textContent = 'Copy', 1200);
    } catch {
      $('copy').textContent = 'Failed';
      setTimeout(() => $('copy').textContent = 'Copy', 1200);
    }
  });

  let isStrict = false;
  $('strict').addEventListener('click', function () {
    if (!output.textContent || output.textContent === '—') return;
    if (isStrict) {
      output.textContent = output.textContent.replace(/\.strict\(\)/g, '');
      $('strict').textContent = 'Make strict';
    } else {
      output.textContent = output.textContent.replace(/\)\s*;?\s*$/, '.strict());');
      $('strict').textContent = 'Undo strict';
    }
    isStrict = !isStrict;
  });
})();
</script>